# The keys a Milō release is signed with, in ssh-keygen's allowed-signers
# format: one key per line, as
#
#   milo-release namespaces="milo-release" ssh-ed25519 <key> <comment>
#
# A unit verifies a release against the copy the release it runs installed
# (/etc/milo/release-signing.pub), before it checks anything out
# (backend/core/updates/release_signature.py), so a key added here is trusted
# from the release after the one that adds it. Rotating is one release, signed
# with the old key, that lists the new key alone (tools/release/sign-release.sh
# --rotate), and every unit must have installed it before a release the new key
# signs is published. A release signed with a key the running release does not
# list is refused by every unit on it. docs/development.md § Signing a release
# has the procedure.
#
# Anyone can verify a release with this file:
#   ssh-keygen -Y verify -f release-signing.pub -I milo-release -n milo-release \
#       -s milo-release-<tag>.manifest.sig < milo-release-<tag>.manifest
milo-release namespaces="milo-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMc2NrQITCKEedX37nERbD08WqjUpPgiQPH9pfzn8SzA milo-release
